<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22241" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-auspĭcātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>At which no auspices were taken</i>, <i>without auspices</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					7, 6, 11</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-auspĭcāto</span></b> , adv. (lit. <i>abl. absol.</i>), <i>without
				consulting the auspices</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod inauspicato pomoerium transgressus esset
					(Ti. Gracchus),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 17, 33</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Of bad omen</i>, <i>unlucky</i>, <i>inauspicious</i> (only post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inauspicatarum animantium vice,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 1, 1, § 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nomen,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 3,
					23, 26, § 145</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exemplum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 7,
					16, 15, § 136</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">garrulitas (cornicis),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 12, 14, § 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bibente conviva mensam tolli inauspicatissimum
					judicatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					28, 2, 5, § 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Unhoped for</i>, <i>unexpected</i>
			(late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">successus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ennod. Ep. 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bona,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
